Origins
-------

The router firmware (Mk2_3phase_RFdatalog_temp) derives from Robin Emley's 3-phase Mk2 PV
Router sketch, Mk2_3phase_RFdatalog_temp_1.ino, the first file of this repository
(2019-10-12). The remote load firmware (RemoteLoadReceiver) derives from his
remoteUnit_fasterControl_1.ino. He published his sketches on the OpenEnergyMonitor forum
(summary page: www.openenergymonitor.org/emon/node/1757) and on www.mk2pvrouter.co.uk,
for others to build PV routers with, without any license statement.

obsolete/ and dev/RST_375us_dev, dev/RST_3phase_free_dev, dev/RawSamplesTool_6chan,
dev/Transformer_Checker and dev/blink_dig4 hold sketches of his, kept for reference.

The changes made since 2019 are by Frédéric Metrich and the contributors listed on
GitHub, under GPL-3.0-or-later.


Your settings
-------------

The files that hold your settings are yours: use, change and share them on any terms you
like. These are, for the router, config.h, config_system.h, config_rf.h and calibration.h,
and for the remote units, config.h and config_rf.h, whether you edit them by hand or the
configurator writes them, and every other file the configurator writes, such as the
ESPHome YAML of the mk2Wifi module. They carry no license tag for that reason.


